<task id="014" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Wire field mapping (step 3) and caller checks on the merged payload; close #1614 and #1617 (FR-06 step 3, FR-08)</title>
    <phase>2 W2 Unified RecordCreationService</phase>
    <gate>002+003+013 complete</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in Sprk.Bff.Api; tags include bff-api, security, authorization; adds tests at KEEP paths (TEST-MODIFYING override); mapped values must never bypass AppendTo (NFR-01).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security boundary: decides which mapped values are written or dropped and must not become an existence oracle or AppendTo bypass.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits the RecordCreationService core that 015 and 016 also edit.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>002, 003, 013</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, security, field-mapping, authorization, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>In `RecordCreationService`, wire step 3 (field mapping: source resolver from task 003, fill-only applier from task 002, canonical engine from task 001) and make step 5 run `CallerWriteAuthorization` on the MERGED payload. A caller-supplied value that fails Create/Append, field security or AppendTo refuses (uniform 404/403, unchanged behaviour). A MAPPED value that fails AppendTo or field security is DROPPED with a warning and the create proceeds. Add the #1614 and #1617 regression tests.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, Dataverse authorization. Follow ADRs strictly; fail closed.</role>
  <goal>Create applies mapping inline in the create request (WP-1, WP-4); every mapped lookup is AppendTo / field-security checked as the caller; the response carries the dropped-value warnings; #1614 and #1617 are closed by tests; the existing `SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*` suite passes unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-06 (step 3, step 4, step 5), FR-08, NFR-01; design.md §4. Today the Office core applies mapping with explicit source only and overwrites, and a regarding-pair mapping skips the caller AppendTo check (#1617); Office Project AppendTo is checked for secure parents only (#1614). Mapped values must be tracked by origin ("caller-supplied" vs "mapped") through steps 3-5 so step 5 can apply different outcomes. The principal's source Read probe (task 003) is already in the resolver; this task only wires it.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.cs (steps 3-5)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CallerWriteAuthorization.cs (only to accept an origin tag per column if needed; existing behaviour for caller-supplied values stays byte-identical)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/FieldMapping/CreateTimeFieldMapping.cs (task 001)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">grep for the mapping-source resolver and FillOnlyMappingApplier symbols under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/FieldMapping/ (tasks 002, 003)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeRecordCreationService.cs (ApplyFieldMappingsAsync - old behaviour to supersede, grep for the symbol)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/MappedValueAuthorizationTests.cs (regression tests for #1614 and #1617 and the drop-with-warning rule)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests.BusinessOwnedAppendTo.cs (fixture style; must pass unchanged)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="002" status="required">Fill-only applier and target guard.</dependency>
      <dependency task="003" status="required">Mapping-source resolver and Read-as-caller probe.</dependency>
      <dependency task="013" status="required">RecordCreationService with the 12-step pipeline and the step 3 seam.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 (path A, spec ADR Tensions)">Scope: payload-dependent authorization. The merged-payload checks stay in `CallerWriteAuthorization` and are called by the service. Do NOT add an endpoint filter that tries to see mapped values. Cite path A in the PR description.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: responses. Warnings and refusals carry stable codes; a dropped mapped value returns a warning code and the column name, never the source record's id, name or any value; no raw exception text.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: identity. Caller checks run as the caller (WhoAmI on the caller token); the create itself stays app-only. System principal reads the mapping source app-only and skips as-caller checks, as in task 013.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI. No new registration; mapping collaborators are static or already registered. If the resolver needs a registration, record it and justify per CLAUDE.md §11.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 (spec)">Scope: all checks added or touched. Fail closed: an error while checking a MAPPED value drops that value with a warning (never writes it); an error while checking a CALLER-SUPPLIED value refuses. A denied or missing mapping source gives the same outcome (no mapped values plus one uniform warning) so it is not an existence oracle. A typed lookup the caller cannot AppendTo still refuses.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: origin tracking. Do not rely on comparing values to detect mapped columns; carry an explicit origin set (caller / mapped) produced by the fill-only applier. A mapped column that the caller also supplied is by definition caller-supplied (fill-only: the caller wins).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: BFF publish. Placement Justification in the PR (BFF write path); fresh-master publish-size delta per §10.4; `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`; no package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added by this task. Integration tests under tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/ (KEEP path); no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;; no DI-registration tests. Cover the stated contract plus the named edge cases only. One seeding proof is requested for the fail-closed guard (temporarily make the merged-payload check a no-op, confirm the #1617 test fails, restore).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Field mapping at create; AppendTo/field-security authorization</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
