      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKE-FIELD-MAPPING-FRAMEWORK.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="polymorphic-resolver" location=".claude/patterns/dataverse/polymorphic-resolver.md">Regarding pair columns the mapping must not target.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor; read spec FR-06/FR-08, NFR-01, issues #1614 and #1617 (gh issue view), and the 002/003/013 outputs; re-grep the step 3 seam in RecordCreationService.</step>
    <step order="1">Run /conflict-check; record the result. Escalate if another PR changes CallerWriteAuthorization or the OwnedChildWrite authorization helpers.</step>
    <step order="2">Write the failing regression tests first (#1617: a mapped regarding-pair or lookup the caller cannot AppendTo is not written and a warning is returned; #1614: Office-style Project under a non-secure parent is AppendTo checked; typed lookup the caller cannot AppendTo still refuses; caller-supplied value survives fill-only; denied source = no mapped values + warning).</step>
    <step order="3">Implement step 3: resolve source (explicit or inferred), probe Read as the caller, read the profile, apply the canonical engine with fill-only semantics, and tag each column with its origin.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement step 5 on the merged payload: run CallerWriteAuthorization for every lookup column; failing caller-supplied columns refuse; failing mapped columns are removed from the payload and a warning is added to the result; then proceed.</step>
    <step order="5">Surface warnings through the service result and the shared ProblemDetails/response shape from task 013 (success responses carry `warnings`; confirm the field already exists on the child-records and Office responses, else record the gap for 017/018 rather than changing a contract here).</step>
    <step order="6">Run the seeding proof described in the ADR-038 constraint; run SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*, RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests and RouteAuthorizationGuardTests unchanged; build; publish-size delta; CVE check.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If dropping a mapped lookup would leave a required column empty (the create would then fail at Dataverse), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 with the table and column; do not choose between refusing and writing.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a mapped value cannot be distinguished from a caller-supplied value at step 5 without changing the CallerWriteAuthorization contract, STOP and escalate before editing it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Grep `ApplyFieldMappingsAsync` in src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeRecordCreationService.cs (explicit source only, overwrite semantics) and `CheckCallerMayCreateAsync` in Services/Dataverse/CallerWriteAuthorization.cs; the new test file has no existing neighbour covering mapped-value authorization (grep "Mapped" under tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership returned none).</existing>
    <extension>Yes for production code: this task extends the service from task 013 and the engine/resolver from 001-003; no new production file. The only new file is a test class, because the existing RecordOwnership suites are ADR-038 KEEP tests that must pass unchanged and should not be edited.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Mapped lookups bypass AppendTo (#1617) and Office Project AppendTo is checked for secure parents only (#1614), so a user can attach a record to a parent they cannot append to through mapping (spec FR-08 acceptance).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test .NET</tool>
    <tool name="gh">Read issues #1614 and #1617</tool>
