  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A mapped lookup the caller cannot AppendTo is NOT written, a warning with a stable code and the column name is returned, and the create succeeds (closes #1617).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A typed (caller-supplied) lookup the caller cannot AppendTo still refuses with the uniform 404/403 outcome; the existing behaviour is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">FR-08 amendment (owner 2026-10-20, UAC-r2 condition c): a MAPPED filing lookup (SecureChildLineage / RecordReparent.FilingParentOf for the target table) that the caller cannot AppendTo REFUSES with the uniform outcome and no create call is issued; must-fire test on a Secure parent, plus a must-not-fire control where a mapped non-filing reference lookup is dropped with a warning.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A mapped value that fails field security is dropped with a warning and the create proceeds; a caller-supplied value that fails field security refuses.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A Project created under a non-secure parent is AppendTo checked as the caller on the merged payload (closes #1614).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A caller-supplied value for a mapped column survives create (fill-only, caller wins); an unsupplied mapped column receives the mapped value in the same create request (no follow-up update).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: when the Read probe on the mapping source is denied, or the source does not exist, the create proceeds with no mapped values and ONE identical warning; the two cases are indistinguishable in status, body and warning text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an exception while checking a mapped value drops that value (never writes it); an exception while checking a caller-supplied value refuses the create with no create call issued.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The seeding proof for the merged-payload check is recorded in the task notes (test fails with the check disabled, passes after restore).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build 0 errors; SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*, RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests and RouteAuthorizationGuardTests pass unchanged; publish-size delta, CVE result and /conflict-check result recorded in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">From task 002 (2026-10-20): the mapping step passes `moneyAttributes` (the target table's Money columns, from attribute metadata) to `CreateTimeFieldMapping.ApplyFillOnly`, so a Default rule into a money column writes a `Money`; test it, then close #2124 (DI-001).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">From task 002 (2026-10-20): `ApplyFillOnly` never writes the regarding pair or resolver fields. Any create whose secure-root filing plan reads a pair that mapping supplied today (Office Project-under-Matter, task 158) gets the pair from the caller or derives it from the filed-under parent BEFORE mapping; SecureRootInheritanceWriterTests.OfficeCreate_* and SecureRootCreateRouteTests.OfficeQuickCreate_* pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">From UAC-r2 D7 / #2169 (2026-10-21):
      - `sprk_document.sprk_accessinheritance` is never a mapping target, at create or on push. It is a BFF-only record of the inherited floor and the document's own narrowing. A rule targeting it is skipped with a per-rule warning reason, matching the push skip. Prefer a protected-target entry on the sprk_document row of RecordTableRules (task 012) over a special case.
      - `sprk_document.sprk_accesspermission` stays fill-only at create, unchanged.
      - Tests: a must-fire case where accessinheritance is skipped at create with its warning, and a must-not-fire case where accesspermission is still filled on an empty new document.
      - UAC-r2 reviews this part of the diff before merge.
    </criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-06 step 3, FR-08, NFR-01. Owner decision 2026-10-19: mapped values that fail AppendTo or field security are skipped with a warning and the create proceeds. Task 015 changes the owner step; do not touch it here.
Completed 2026-10-21.
- What landed: mapping is opt-in per request (RecordCreationRequest.Mapping) and fill-only; the source is probed for the caller's Read first; moneyAttributes and protected sets are honoured; caller checks run on the merged payload by origin; a mapped filing lookup refuses; other mapped failures drop with record_creation.mapped_value_dropped; a server-set filing lookup is asked AppendTo before the plan (new code record_creation.server_set_filing_lookup); D7 accessinheritance is never mapped; ebilling items 1-3 are met.
- Reviews: two opus passes, every F fixed. Pass 2 caught a pre-plan ordering existence oracle.
- Tests: 134 in the task test classes; mutants M1-M18 killed except M12 (equivalent).
